  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`, `onOpen`: the header writes the machine name through the post's own `clean()`. `(`, `)`, `%` and `;` become a space. The name is cut to 40 characters. This is the rule of `fanuc.cps` and `fanuc-lathe.cps` (#594).\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`, `oWord()`: a program number below 1 or above 9999 is refused by name. The text is the text of `fanuc.cps`: `program number 10000 is outside O0001-O9999, the control's program numbers`. The old code clamped the number to O9999.\n- `oWord()` reads the number with `isNaN`, not with `|| 1`. Thus a program number of 0 is refused. Before, it became O0001.\n- `crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs` (the #594 suite):\n  - `doosan-dnm` joins the dialect list of `hostile_names_post_well_formed_comments_in_every_mill_dialect`.\n  - New pin `doosan_dnm_header_cleans_the_name_and_refuses_a_number_past_o9999`.\n- `docs/decisions/4349-dnm-header-name-onumber.md`: the decision record.\n\n## Cause\n\n- `onOpen` wrote `\"(\" + nm + \")\"` with the raw `machine.name`. `DNM 5700 (5AX) 100%` gave `O0001 (DNM 5700 (5AX) 100%)`: a nested comment, and a `%` that ends the tape.\n- `oWord()` did `Math.max(1, Math.min(n, 9999))`. The engine sets `programNumber` from the document (`crates/post/src/post/js.rs` `set_program`). A document number of 10000 posted as `O9999`, which is another program.\n\nNew output: `O0001 (DNM 5700 5AX 100)`. Program number 10000 or 0: the post is refused with the message above. Program number 9999: `O9999 (DNM)`.\n\n## Tests (final head, against upstream/main 79f4dbe4a)\n\n- Pins:\n  - `doosan_dnm_header_cleans_the_name_and_refuses_a_number_past_o9999`\n  - `hostile_names_post_well_formed_comments_in_every_mill_dialect` (now with `doosan-dnm`)\n- Red before the fix: yes. On unchanged code the two pins failed: `left: Some(\"O0001 (DNM 5700 (5AX) 100%)\")` and `doosan-dnm: unbalanced or nested comment \"O0001 (MSG, Mill (A); B*)\"`.\n- Mutations (each one alone, then restored):\n  - `clean(nm)` back to `nm`: the two pins fail.\n  - Range guard removed: the new pin fails (`program number 0 must be refused`).\n  - Only the upper bound removed (`n < 1`): the new pin fails (`program number 10000 must be refused`).\n  - `isNaN` back to `|| 1`: the new pin fails (`program number 0 must be refused`).\n  - Fix restored: all pass.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test comment_escape --test doosan_dnm_post --test script_doosan_dnm`: 5 + 9 + 11 passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 73 steps, 0 failed. This includes `app suites: example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `conformance` and `doosan_dnm_a_state`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: 2 steps (release build, `app heavy: probe_no_coolant`), 0 failed.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: 6 steps (motion light: lib, three adaptive_troch twins; app light: pocket_pass_start), 0 failed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. I ran the example catalog suites, `conformance` and `script_doosan_dnm`. They passed. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" \"examples/catalog/**\"` is empty. The shipped Doosan machine name (`Doosan DNM 5700 + rotary table`) has no character that `clean()` changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The program was not run on a Doosan control.\n- A machine name longer than 40 characters is now cut to 40. No shipped machine has such a name. No test pins the cut for this post; the #594 suite pins it for the sister posts.\n- `fanuc.cps` `progNo()` also uses `|| 1`, so a program number of 0 becomes O0001 there. This PR does not change `fanuc.cps`. The engine's document number is normally 1 or more.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #4363 changes `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps` in other functions (`endPreamble`, `onLinear`, `onCircular`). It touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #2646 changes `crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs` in a different test (`header_notes_use_each_shipped_dialect_and_keep_the_full_surface_bound`). Same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Doosan DNM post: the header cleans the machine name (no nested parentheses, no `%`), and a program number outside O0001-O9999 is refused by name instead of becoming O9999.\n\nFixes #4349\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
